        "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
        "outdated": true,
        "path": "reflex/utils/exec.py",
        "first_comment": "In dev mode with Granian (the default whenever uvicorn or gunicorn isn't installed), `App running at:` is never printed now. Nothing replaces it later either: the backend announces itself only through `Backend running at:`.\n\nTools outside this repo parse that line. `docs/enterprise/testing.md:318` says the reflex-enterprise pytest plugin builds `reflex_app.url`, including `frontend_path`, by reading reflex's own \"App running at:\" line, and its default `run_mode` is dev. That plugin would stop finding the URL. reflex-bench needed a regex change in this PR for the same reason. The PR's own test confirms the line is gone: `test_exec.py:177-178` asserts `\"App running at:\" not in message` for granian with a backend.\n\nFix: keep the `App running at:` text. One option is to print the frontend line as before and only move the backend line to lifespan startup. If the rename has to stay, treat it as a breaking change for log parsers, with a deprecation path.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https",
        "at": "2026-10-08T20:39:03Z"
      }
    ]
  },
